  "findings": [
    "R1 known-cost source/export/setup infrastructure failures now stop local/shared health before the next arm while preserving actual known usage. Ordinary model-semantic outcomes remain distinct.",
    "Explicit infrastructure or persistence flags bar complete status even on the final arm; regression retains both arms actual costs and marks pair incomplete.",
    "Both arms share discovery retention, budget and provider policies, differing in eager versus demand visibility; task/repetition order remains balanced.",
    "Native episode admission and bounded transport callbacks check shared health and storage before dispatch. Error paths preserve merged receipts and unknown reservations through pair persistence failures.",
    "Successful orchestration result is reused by verified path/hash instead of duplicated. Synthetic integration exercises local Git, native bounded recycler and both-arm native export."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Candidate-only approval: prospective global runner still must enforce source/evidence allocation, transport settlement and fixed full-campaign slots.",
    "Pair window_admission_valid is count/numerical metadata, not independent request digest reconstruction; exact live admission and scorer bindings remain required.",
    "Inherited accountReceipts relies on transport dispatch flags; final trajectory validator must reject contradictory undispatched positive-spend receipts.",
    "No actual providers, quality scores or efficiency claims follow from synthetic tests."
  ],
